  description: The Sun is the star at the center of our Solar System and contains
    most of its total mass. Its gravity keeps the planets in orbit, while the energy
    produced by nuclear fusion provides Earth with the light and warmth essential
    for life.
  interestingFact: Light from the Sun takes approximately eight minutes and twenty
    seconds to travel the 150 million kilometers to Earth.
